{"kind":"artifact","text":"The OpenTelemetry boundary at internal/telemetry on repair head b966b0f4. Behaviour is unchanged; the privacy evidence is not. TestInMemoryExporterGetsTemplateOnlyHTTPMetrics now inspects span event attributes and every collected metric datapoint attribute, because Record attaches operation attributes with AddEvent and they never reach span.Attributes, which is all the previous assertion read. It also counts what it inspected and requires the bounded http.route to be present in both places, so a walk that found nothing cannot pass quietly. Verified by mutation: routing the raw URL path into the observer now fails this package, where before it stayed green while internal/observe caught the same mutation; suppressing the route attributes entirely also fails it.","body":{"commit":"b966b0f499aace6120f9c2ff01ab48211e59d489","path":"internal/telemetry"}}